@startuml lease-at-launch
!theme plain
title Legacy readable-token view: Slice 0: curator-run verifies the caller-composed plan and protected binding, leases and starts Claude

participant "curator-run\n(agent OS account, uid 30412)" as E
participant "swarma-credential-broker\nunprivileged broker service UID" as B
participant "Harness\nClaude Code, agent OS account" as H

E -> E: verify caller-composed plan; no profile resolution\nresolve protected credential_binding/1 (CIP-0010 C3.4):\nprofile, harness, account, channel, endpoint,\nexecutable digest, policy generation
E -> E: refuse if another credential source is present\n(credential_source_conflict)
E -> E: verify destination-local network binding from composed plan\nrecord {profile_ref, profile_digest, assurance: cooperative}\ndeclared evidence only, not enforcement or platform admission
E -> B: connect; check the server's peer UID is the broker's
E -> B: lease.request {harness, profile, account, channel: env,\ncredential_binding, network, launch_id}
B -> B: under the state lock: require verifiable admission class; refuse untrusted class;\nrefuse R-ALLSTOP freeze or fenced restore;\n1 peer = agent principal of an active, unexpired binding (ledger 4a91c5e03b2d4788a649d70fc62e15bd active)\n2 lease chain and caller chain verify current revocations and R-TIME max/min windows\n3 leaf covers account, harness, profile; profile in binding\n4 account active, known expiry checked, harness matches\n5 channel valid; harness release qualified\n6 binding fields match; endpoint and executable approved\n7 network: cooperative assurance match recorded as declared evidence only
alt any check fails
  B --> E: typed refusal; class/freeze codes unpublished;\nother check codes include lease_not_authorised / lease_binding_mismatch
  E -> E: do not exec; report
else admission-class/freeze gates and all checks pass
  B --> E: lease/1 {lease_id, payload, token_expires_at, authorized_until}
  E -> E: re-check the binding tuple and conflicts
  E -> H: exec with CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN in the process environment only\n(not argv, not files, not logs)
  note over E,H
    Successful exec replaces curator-run; no return on harness exit.
    Close-on-exec broker connection closes (§4.1); disconnect is not release.
    Env harness does not talk to broker; no post-exec release/report (§8.5).
  end note
end
note over E,H: Readable-token exception: Claude can read/copy its own token.\ncredential-injection/1 requires effective-source and child-inheritance qualification;\nthis sequence is a design contract, not qualification evidence.
note over B
  Broker owns account/secret, grant/revocation, binding and lease files;
  helper owns the root ledger. Lease records contain no payload (§8.3).
  [[../spec/broker.md#82-checks-in-order Spec §8.2]]
  [[lease-recovery.puml M-CB2: refusal, disconnect and recovery branches]]
end note
note over B,H
  env: renewal refused after authorized_until; revocation stops new
  leases/renewals; R-ALLSTOP freezes all leases/renewals; unbind ends leases (§6.4, §7.2, §8.5).
  Release before exec vs retain until that limit: unspecified in spec §18.7.
  stdin: surviving client and release point unspecified in spec §18.7.
  external-token: live executor / later runner holds lease and can release;
  teardown timing / failure cleanup unspecified in spec §18.7 (§9.3).
  Record expiry scheduling is unpublished; copied token ends only with
  token expiry or vendor revocation, not broker release (§12.1).
  [[../spec/broker.md#85-renewal-release-and-reports Spec §8.5]]
end note
note over E,H
  Claude has no refresh: swarma-operator re-enrols through operator command;
  phone-signed or password-sudo act (timestamp_timeout=0, no NOPASSWD),
  with exact content confirmation; refused inside agent sessions (§14).
  Executor restarts; --resume (§10.1).
  Unreadable revocations or fenced restore refuse (§6.4, §15.4).
  Prior dispatcher revocation.check cannot waive final broker checks.
  Cleanup after a post-lease tuple/conflict refusal is unspecified in spec §12.2.
end note
note over B
  R-TIME: expiry/authorized_until checked at max(now, watermark);
  not_before = min(now, watermark); untrusted time refuses delivery (§15.1).
  Expired binding unusable even while elapsed-removal gate retains its record.
  R-REBIND ends old leases; copied env token keeps only vendor lifetime.
  Platform admission: static R-RANGE-DENY fence + provider-only binding;
  cooperative assurance is declared evidence only, never that admission proof.
  R-NETBIND v1: machine-owned network policy pinned at admission;
  fw.apply verifies listener serves the applied digest (§5.5).
end note
note over E,B
  R-UNTRUSTED: no binding or lease for untrusted-class accounts.
  Unavailable class evidence also refuses; encoding/codes unpublished (§18.16).
  R-ALLSTOP is durable, checked before delivery; explicit recovery only.
  Partial/unknown recovery keeps admission closed; delivered tokens
  keep vendor lifetime (§15.5). Freeze code/record formats unpublished (§18.17).
end note
@enduml

@startuml lease-at-launch-secret-free
!theme plain
title Proposed secret-free view: lease-at-launch — inactive
participant "Runner / harness\nagent account" as A
participant "Separate injecting gateway" as G
participant "Minimal broker" as B
participant "Qualified provider" as P
A -> A : selected secret-free mode; qualified endpoint/channel\nprotected source/plan/child checks; no alternate login
G -> B : own admitted service lease for account
B --> G : real vendor material; agent receives none
G --> A : random per-lease placeholder; generation / launch / account bound
A -> G : request on own listener with placeholder
G -> G : current service lease AND original caller chain\nactual operation/resource/account; class/policy/hold/stop checks\nmatch agent plaintext BEFORE legitimate injection
alt all qualified and current
  G -> P : own guarded dial + authenticated TLS; attach credential
  P --> G : response
  G --> A : response only if no credential reflection
else source/authority/matcher/listener/route conflict
  G --> A : refuse; no upstream credential attachment
end
note over A,P
  Placeholder outside own listener is useless; port reuse grants nothing.
  Enforced network/IPC boundary denies direct provider/store/other listener.
  Endpoint mode only; TLS interception CLOSED, no exposed fallback by failure.
end note

legend bottom
  Separate proposed secret-free mode, document revision 1: INACTIVE / UNQUALIFIED.
  Semantic responsibilities only; no new v0 methods, fields, codes or record formats.
  [[../spec/secret-free-mode.md Owning proposed contract and qualification gates]]
endlegend
@enduml
